Notebook[{
Cell["One Postulate in Wolfram", "Title"],
Cell["This workbook is a computational companion to paper/one-postulate.tex. It follows the paper's kappa-controlled story, but it does not replace the Lean proof surface.", "Text"],
Cell["Introduction", "Section"],
Cell["The paper's core claim is structural: the relativity principle leads to a one-parameter family of kinematics, and the Killing form separates that family into Euclidean, Galilean, and Lorentzian branches.", "Text"],
Cell["The notebook keeps proof authority with the local Lean files and uses Wolfram Language only for symbolic exploration.", "Text"],
Cell["The kappa-controlled commutator family", "Section"],
Cell["ClearAll[t, x, v, kappa, gamma, tPrime, xPrime, killing, boostBlock, spacetimeMetric, c]", "Input"],
Cell["gamma = 1/Sqrt[1 - kappa v^2]", "Input"],
Cell["tPrime = gamma (t - kappa v x)", "Input"],
Cell["xPrime = gamma (x - v t)", "Input"],
Cell["Limit[gamma, kappa -> 0]", "Input"],
Cell["{Limit[tPrime, kappa -> 0], Limit[xPrime, kappa -> 0]}", "Input"],
Cell["Explicit bracket calculations", "Section"],
Cell["The ordered basis is (Jx, Jy, Jz, Kx, Ky, Kz). The symbolic checkpoint matches the paper's adopted homogeneous kinematics algebra.", "Text"],
Cell["boostBlock = 4 kappa IdentityMatrix[3]", "Input"],
Cell["killing = DiagonalMatrix[Join[ConstantArray[-4, 3], ConstantArray[4 kappa, 3]]]", "Input"],
Cell["MatrixForm[killing]", "Input"],
Cell["Killing form computation", "Section"],
Cell["The decisive fact is that the rotation block stays nonzero while the boost block scales with kappa.", "Text"],
Cell["Det[killing]", "Input"],
Cell["Eigenvalues[killing]", "Input"],
Cell["Boost-sector and spacetime consequences", "Section"],
Cell["spacetimeMetric = DiagonalMatrix[{1, -kappa, -kappa, -kappa}]", "Input"],
Cell["MatrixForm[spacetimeMetric]", "Input"],
Cell["c = 1/Sqrt[kappa]", "Input"],
Cell["Limit[c, kappa -> 0, Direction -> \"FromAbove\"]", "Input"],
Cell["Branch comparison", "Section"],
Cell["Grid[{{\"Regime\", \"Symbolic consequence\", \"Paper interpretation\"}, {\"kappa < 0\", \"boost block negative definite; no real singular speed\", \"Euclidean branch\"}, {\"kappa = 0\", \"boost block vanishes; Galilean limit holds\", \"Galilean branch\"}, {\"kappa > 0\", \"finite real singular speed at 1/Sqrt[kappa]\", \"Lorentzian branch\"}}, Frame -> All]", "Input"],
Cell["Lean crosswalk", "Section"],
Cell["The notebook's symbolic checkpoints correspond to Lean modules and theorems, but Lean remains the proof authority.", "Text"],
Cell["Grid[{{\"Notebook topic\", \"Lean anchor\"}, {\"Transformation law and Galilean limit\", \"OnePostulate/SpacetimeMatrices.lean\"}, {\"Bracket family\", \"matrix_bracket_JJ / matrix_bracket_JK / matrix_bracket_KK; kinematic_bracket_table\"}, {\"Killing form\", \"killing_form_diag; boost_killing_form_eq\"}, {\"Boost and spacetime branches\", \"killing_restricts_to_metric; spacetime_metric_invariant; phase1_selection_summary\"}}, Frame -> All]", "Input"],
Cell["Proof authority note", "Section"],
Cell["Computed or symbolically checked here means that the notebook evaluates formulas it already states. Formalized in Lean means that the repository proves the corresponding claims in the Lean modules. The notebook never widens the proof surface.", "Text"]
},
WindowTitle -> "One Postulate in Wolfram",
StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"
]
